course: dictionary
lesson: 918
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «The blast threw hot rock into the sky.» Hot rock flying up into the sky means blast is an explosion here.
explain: «In deserts wind blasts sand against rocks and carves strange shapes.» The word is the same, but the clues are wind, sand and rocks, so blast means a strong rush of wind here.
explain: «The trumpet call is air blasted out through the trunk.» Blasted means pushed out hard and fast, so the sound is loud. Always try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
fact: A blast can be an explosion, a strong rush of wind or air, or a very loud sound.
fact: To blast means to blow up with explosives, or to play music very loudly.
fact: «Blast off» means a rocket takes off.
fact: «Have a blast» is informal and means a great, fun time.
fact: «Blast!» is a mild stand-in for a swear word, like «drat», «sugar» or «darn».
exercise: «The blast was billions of times stronger than the biggest bomb ever made.» What is a blast here? | A tidy bedroom | A gentle whisper | *An explosion | A cool breeze on a summer day
exercise: «The room filled with a blast of cold air when the door opened.» What is a blast of cold air? | A very loud sound from a horn | A rocket taking off | *A sudden strong rush of air | A kind of sweet
exercise: «We will have a blast at the party!» What does have a blast mean? | Be blown up | *Have a great, fun time | Play a trumpet | Take off into space
test: «Mum shouted, "Blast!" when she dropped the milk.» What does the word blast show about Mum? | *She is annoyed, and it is a mild stand-in for a swear word | She is playing a trumpet loudly | She is very happy about the spilt milk | She is starting a rocket
test: In «blast off», what happens? | Music gets quieter | A door blows shut | A horn sounds softly | *A rocket takes off
exam: In «The horn gave one long blast», what does blast mean? | A tiny drop of rain | A rocket taking off | An explosion of rock | *A very loud sound
